        "abstract": "Microengineering technologies are being rapidly applied to make precise connections between optical components and fibres, and between fibres. Anisotropic etching of silicon enables the accurate fabrication of V-shaped grooves to locate optic fibres. Single mode fibres can be positioned using microfabricated clips 3 micron thick with a clipping force of 10 Nm/sup -1/. This demountable technology enables low cost assembly without the need for active alignment.",
